{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumUniverses.FrobeniusPairingUnique","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumUniverses.FrobeniusPairingUnique","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Simple","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Preadditive.Schur","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Preadditive"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobeniusForm_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobeniusForm_unique","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-pairing-unique.lean#L113-L128","doc":"**Uniqueness of the Frobenius pairing up to scalar (conditional).**\n\nWrapper over `frobeniusForm_unique_axiom`: on a simple common\nobject the Frobenius form is determined up to an invertible scalar\nin `End(𝟙)`.  Replaces the false `Subsingleton (FrobeniusHopfData\nC)` claim originally written here. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:frobenius-pairing-unique","label":"prop:frobenius-pairing-unique","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-pairing-unique.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobeniusForm_unique_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobeniusForm_unique_axiom","kind":"axiom","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-pairing-unique.lean#L92-L111","doc":"**Frobenius form unique up to invertible scalar (conditional,\nnamed categorical input).**\n\nOn a *simple* common object, two `FrobeniusHopfData` Frobenius\nforms differ by an invertible scalar `c : End(𝟙_ C)` (post-\ncomposed, after transporting along the object equality).  The\nsimplicity hypothesis is essential — it drops to multi-block in a\nsemisimple but non-simple category.  This is the §3b-cond\nconditional content (Schur 1-dimensionality of `Hom(A, 𝟙)`,\n[kock2004]); it replaces a false `Subsingleton (FrobeniusHopfData\nC)` axiom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobeniusForm_unique_of_schur","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobeniusForm_unique_of_schur","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-pairing-unique.lean#L63-L90","doc":"**Uniqueness of the Frobenius form up to an invertible scalar, proved\nunder Schur hypotheses.**\n\nIf `C` is preadditive with kernels and monoidal-preadditive, and both the\ncommon object and the tensor unit are simple, then each Frobenius form\n`A ⟶ 𝟙` is nonzero, hence an isomorphism by Schur's lemma, and\n`c := (e ≫ λ₂)⁻¹ ≫ λ₁` is the required invertible scalar.\n\nThis is the axiom below with its missing hypotheses made explicit. The\naxiom itself carries no linear structure and no simplicity of `𝟙`; whether\nit holds without them is open (bean `qou-n2un`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobeniusForm_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobeniusForm_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-pairing-unique.lean#L51-L61","doc":"A Frobenius form is nonzero whenever its object is simple: if `λ = 0`\nthen `ev = μ ≫ λ = 0`, and the left snake identity makes `𝟙_A = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}